{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1574 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "218cbf072ebd058bc57dacf39622295bc518a1fc48f482b9bc42045918ad86a0" :edb/db-before-t 1573 :edb/db-after-t 1574 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534886 50 #inst "2026-10-12T22:27:58.998Z" 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186231429 1038 #edb/ref 17592186442740 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186316816 1078 #edb/ref 17592186316277 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186316816 1078 #edb/ref 17592186441790 13194139534886 17592186045417 false] [17592186317431 1071 "A particle is moving with forced harmonic motion without damping. The particle is acted on by an external periodic force\n$f(t)=-12\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t).$\nAssuming the system experiences resonance, which of the following could be used to represent the general solution for the position $y(t)?$\n\n- $y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t+ϕ)+\\frac{1}{2}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$\n- $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t+ϕ)+\\frac{1}{2}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$\n- $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)+\\frac{1}{2}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$\n\nNote that $A,$ $B,$ $R,$ and $ϕ$ are constants." 13194139534886 17592186045417 false] [17592186317431 1071 "A particle is moving with forced harmonic motion without damping. The particle is acted on by an external periodic force\n$f(t)=-12\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t).$\nAssuming the system experiences resonance, which of the following could be used to represent the general solution for the position $y(t)?$\n\nI. $y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t+ϕ)+\\frac{1}{2}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$\n\nII. $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t+ϕ)+\\frac{1}{2}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$\n\nIII. $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)+\\frac{1}{2}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$\n\nNote that $A,$ $B,$ $R,$ and $ϕ$ are constants." 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186317431 1074 "Because the motion is undamped and the system experiences resonance, the forcing frequency equals the natural frequency $\\omega .$\n\nThe external force is $f(t)=-12\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t),$ which is sinusoidal with frequency $3.$ Therefore,\n$\\omega =3.$\n\nThe complementary solution for the associated simple harmonic motion equation can be written in three different forms:\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\omega t+ϕ)=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t+ϕ)$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\omega t+ϕ)=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t+ϕ)$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$\n\nAt resonance, a sinusoidal trial at frequency $\\omega $ duplicates the complementary solution, so we multiply by $t$ and take a resonant particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=t(C\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+D\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)).\n$$\n\nBy substituting the particular solution and $\\omega =3$ into the differential equation, ${y}^{″}+{\\omega }^{2}y=f(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[(6D-9Ct)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-(6C+9Dt)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)]+9t(C\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+D\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)) & =-12\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ 6D\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-6C\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) & =-12\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating coefficients, $C=\\frac{1}{2}$ and $D=-2.$ \n\nSo, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=\\frac{1}{2}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t).\n$$\n\nFinally, then, the general solution is given by the sum of the complementary and particular solutions. So, it can be written in any of the following forms:\n\n- $y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t+ϕ)+\\frac{1}{2}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$\n\n- $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t+ϕ)+\\frac{1}{2}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$\n\n- $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)+\\frac{1}{2}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$\n\nSolutions I, II, and III match the forms above.\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\"." 13194139534886 17592186045417 false] [17592186317431 1074 "Because the motion is undamped and the system experiences resonance, the forcing frequency equals the natural frequency $\\omega .$\n\nThe external force is $f(t)=-12\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t),$ which is sinusoidal with frequency $3.$ Therefore,\n$\\omega =3.$\n\nThe complementary solution for the associated simple harmonic motion equation can be written in three different forms:\n\n1\\. ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\omega t+ϕ)=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t+ϕ)$\n\n2\\. ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\omega t+ϕ)=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t+ϕ)$\n\n3\\. ${y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$\n\nAt resonance, a sinusoidal trial at frequency $\\omega $ duplicates the complementary solution, so we multiply by $t$ and take a resonant particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=t(C\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+D\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)).\n$$\n\nBy substituting the particular solution and $\\omega =3$ into the differential equation, ${y}^{″}+{\\omega }^{2}y=f(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[(6D-9Ct)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-(6C+9Dt)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)]+9t(C\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+D\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)) & =-12\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ 6D\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-6C\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) & =-12\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating coefficients, $C=\\frac{1}{2}$ and $D=-2.$ \n\nSo, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=\\frac{1}{2}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t).\n$$\n\nFinally, then, the general solution is given by the sum of the complementary and particular solutions. So, it can be written in any of the following forms:\n\n1\\. $y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t+ϕ)+\\frac{1}{2}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$\n\n2\\. $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t+ϕ)+\\frac{1}{2}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$\n\n3\\. $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)+\\frac{1}{2}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$\n\nSolutions I, II, and III match the forms above.\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\"." 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186435710 1075 #edb/ref 17592186442733 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186435710 1078 #edb/ref 17592186435697 13194139534886 17592186045417 false] [17592186435710 1078 #edb/ref 17592186442733 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442732 1043 #edb/ref 17592186442741 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442732 1043 #edb/ref 17592186442742 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442732 1043 #edb/ref 17592186442743 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442732 1043 #edb/ref 17592186442744 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442732 1043 #edb/ref 17592186442745 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442732 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442732 1045 "Resonance in Vibrating Systems" 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442732 1046 #edb/ref 17592186442742 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442732 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046660 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442732 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048966 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442732 1053 #uuid "d9d2f46d-5baa-5bef-85ef-5cb27486297b" 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442733 1080 "4.5" 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442733 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442733 1083 #uuid "065c1236-c8cd-5e0a-8536-ab48d1fe6aae" 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442734 1080 "I only" 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442734 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442734 1083 #uuid "10ac45f2-8682-5e38-90a5-af6b3b0df052" 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442735 1080 "I and II only" 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442735 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442735 1083 #uuid "720de89b-25be-516b-9df5-32bca90894e6" 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442736 1080 "II only" 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442736 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442736 1083 #uuid "8b3b3ddc-f2b0-5960-a120-6e3182615388" 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442737 1080 "III only" 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442737 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442737 1083 #uuid "90774d44-8df7-5a01-b829-eff4553b5ba9" 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442738 1080 "I and III only" 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442738 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442738 1083 #uuid "eb5401b3-3249-566f-8e5f-01020ae0590b" 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442739 1075 #edb/ref 17592186442734 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442739 1075 #edb/ref 17592186442735 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442739 1075 #edb/ref 17592186442736 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442739 1075 #edb/ref 17592186442737 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442739 1075 #edb/ref 17592186442738 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442739 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442739 1077 "selection" 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442739 1078 #edb/ref 17592186442736 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442739 1079 #uuid "c3260424-876c-50ae-ac8b-7b96731c9907" 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442740 1068 #edb/ref 17592186442739 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442740 1069 "q-343743" 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442740 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442740 1071 "A particle is moving with forced harmonic motion without damping. The particle is acted on by an external periodic force\n$f(t)=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t).$\nAssuming the system experiences resonance, which of the following could be used to represent the general solution for the position $y(t)?$\n\nI. $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t+ϕ)+\\frac{2}{3}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$\n\nII. $y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t+ϕ)-\\frac{2}{3}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)$\n\nIII. $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$\n\nNote that $A,$ $B,$ $R,$ and $ϕ$ are constants." 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442740 1072 #uuid "ee642054-1d27-50a4-8f05-345ca578dfc0" 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442740 1074 "Because the motion is undamped and the system experiences resonance, the forcing frequency equals the natural frequency $\\omega .$\n\nThe external force is $f(t)=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t),$ which is sinusoidal with frequency $3.$ Therefore,\n$\\omega =3.$\n\nThe complementary solution for the associated simple harmonic motion equation can be written in three different forms:\n\n1\\. ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\omega t+ϕ)=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t+ϕ)$\n\n2\\. ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\omega t+ϕ)=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t+ϕ)$\n\n3\\. ${y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$\n\nAt resonance, a sinusoidal trial at frequency $\\omega $ duplicates the complementary solution, so we multiply by $t$ and take a resonant particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=t(C\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+D\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)).\n$$\n\nBy substituting the particular solution and $\\omega =3$ into the differential equation, ${y}^{″}+{\\omega }^{2}y=f(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[9(D-Ct)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-9(C+Dt)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)]+9t(C\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+D\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)) & =4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ 9D\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-9C\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) & =4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating coefficients, $C=-\\frac{2}{3}$ and $D=0.$ \n\nSo, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=-\\frac{2}{3}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t).\n$$\n\nFinally, then, the general solution is given by the sum of the complementary and particular solutions. So, it can be written in any of the following forms:\n\n1\\. $y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t+ϕ)-\\frac{2}{3}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)$\n\n2\\. $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t+ϕ)-\\frac{2}{3}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)$\n\n3\\. $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)-\\frac{2}{3}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)$\n\nOnly solution II matches the forms above. Therefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"." 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442741 1058 #edb/ref 17592186442743 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442741 1062 #uuid "102631d9-03a3-5a77-8b43-d3ebf3037f1b" 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442741 1063 #edb/ref 17592186435720 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442742 1058 #edb/ref 17592186442744 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442742 1062 #uuid "5ee37f4e-428d-5c80-b898-6258e65e6514" 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442742 1063 #edb/ref 17592186317422 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442743 1062 #uuid "63616043-21be-5d80-99e6-bbe839235312" 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442743 1063 #edb/ref 17592186317431 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442744 1058 #edb/ref 17592186442745 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442744 1062 #uuid "83ab17b5-350b-529d-97cb-ee01d416ef71" 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [17592186442744 1063 #edb/ref 17592186435716 13194139534886 17592186045417 true] [1759218644